  "comments": [],
  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "People in a Kazakh village kept falling asleep for days mid-sentence. Starting in 2013, residents of Kalachi would black out without warning. They woke up days later with zero memory of what happened.",
        "visual_query": "rural village steppe northern kazakhstan",
        "visual_fallback": "foggy small town"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Animals were affected too. Cats hallucinated and dogs collapsed mid-bark. Doctors checked for viruses, radiation, and contaminated water, but every single test came back completely normal.",
        "visual_query": "vintage hospital hallway medical lab equipment",
        "visual_fallback": "medical lab environment"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Could an invisible threat be wiping out a town's consciousness? By 2015, over a hundred people had fallen victim to the sudden sleeping fits, turning Kalachi into a ghost town.",
        "visual_query": "empty quiet streets remote kazakhstan town",
        "visual_fallback": "empty desolate town"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The answer lay underground in an abandoned Soviet uranium mine. During specific weather shifts, high levels of carbon monoxide seeped into the valley, suffocating the town without them noticing.",
        "visual_query": "abandoned soviet mine entrance kazakhstan",
        "visual_fallback": "abandoned industrial mine"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The odorless gas displaced oxygen in the air, essentially forcing human brains into survival hibernation before anyone could smell a thing.",
        "visual_query": "steam rising over snowy kazakhstan landscape",
        "visual_fallback": "mysterious rising fog"
      }
    ],
